<!-- ============ 10. GLOSSARY ============ -->
<h1 class="section" id="s10">10. Glossary</h1>
<table>
<tr><th>Term</th><th>Definition</th></tr>
<tr><td>Fayda ID</td><td>Ethiopia's national digital identity system, used for authenticating farmers and submitters within OAN.</td></tr>
<tr class="alt"><td>Grievance</td><td>A formally recorded complaint or issue raised by a submitter concerning an agricultural service or transaction.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Submitter</td><td>Any entity authorized to lodge a grievance: individual farmer, cooperative, FPO, NGO, or Woreda/Kebele body.</td></tr>
<tr class="alt"><td>Service Category</td><td>A classification of grievances based on domain (Inputs, Schemes, Payments, Credit, Markets).</td></tr>
<tr><td>SLA</td><td>Service Level Agreement &ndash; the expected timeframe within which an assigned agency must act on a grievance.</td></tr>
<tr class="alt"><td>Nodal Officer</td><td>Central administrator responsible for manual routing and oversight of unrouted or escalated grievances.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ticket Number</td><td>Unique, human-readable identifier generated at submission (e.g. OROM-BISH-AGRN-12345).</td></tr>
<tr class="alt"><td>Woreda / Kebele</td><td>Ethiopian sub-regional administrative units used for geographic classification of grievances.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Overlay flag</td><td>A boolean state (escalated, anonymized) that coexists with, and never replaces, the canonical grievance status.</td></tr>
</table>

<h1 class="section" id="s11">11. Open Questions</h1>
<p>Consolidated from &sect;5 and &sect;8. Items resolved by checking the FRS directly are marked so they aren't re-raised; the rest genuinely need an answer from someone outside this document.</p>

